      "title": "RKLB Q3 Earnings Call Highlights Neutron Demand and Launch Delays",
      "summary": "Rocket Lab reported Q3 revenues of $267.83M (73% YoY growth, beating estimates) but posted a wider-than-expected loss of 7 cents per share. The company secured $1B in new launch contracts, boosting backlog to $3.57B, with improved pricing power. However, Neutron's first launch shifted to 2027 due to manufacturing defects. The pending Iridium acquisition is fully financed with shareholder approval, though regulatory approval remains pending. Cash flow remains pressured despite positive GAAP operating cash flow of $7.2M.",
